> I have had this problem with DU 4.0D a few times now, and I managed to
> confuse the hell out of DEC Support, so I was wondering if anyone else
> has had this problem. Basically, after a clean install of 4.0D, on a
> Alphastation 500, I tried using dxkerneltuner to alter vm-vpagemax, and
> maxusers parameters, (Although it doesnt seem to matter what parameters
> get changed), and upon save and exit, the sysconfigtab file is
> Corrupted, having binary information appended to it, (making it about
> 64K). I found that I could recreate the problem, by copying the
> sysconfigtab file prior to editing, then going back, and changing random
> parameters. Each and every time, the same result. However, after using
> chvol to alter the dirty blocks cache on the root_domain, the problem
> disappears. If I then alter this back to its original value, it still
> does not re-appear. I only seem to be able to recreate the problem after
> a clean install, but it has happened on about 3 different occasions,
> after installation.
> 
> Anyone else experienced similar problems with dxkerneltuner?.

Seems more or less of an AdvFS domain problem or a bad disk, not a
dxkerneltuner problem. Try something with sysconfig / sysconfigdb like:

# sysconfig -q vm maxusers > foo
# sysconfigdb -a -f foo vm

-y.

