4.0D is supposed to be Y2K compliant. It has a small issue over "at" not
recognizing 29-02-2000 as an existing date (leap year), so anything placed for
execution at that day will run on 01-03-2000. "The latest Service Pack has that
bug fixed". Well, the latest is SP5 and a lot of people are complaining about
it. A consensus is that SP3 for DU 4.0D fixes it, although I can't see any patch
kits referring to "at" in the SP3.

Generally, avoid SP5 if you can, all UNIX versions. It is big (20-30 Megs bigger
than SP4, why?), it makes problems.

Nix.



