Larry Buss wrote:
> 
> I did forget to mention that screens 0.1 and 0.2 are black upon login and
> the mouse tracks to the other screens. How can I get the backgrounds, front
> panel, etc to display on these screens?
> 
> Thanks again for the help
> 
> -LB
> 

The front panel is on other heads with Tru64 5.0 (supposedly).

CDE is a bit crippled wrt multihead.  Check the dt.resources file
builds for you under $HOME/.dt/...  It *sets* the number of workspaces
on other heads to 1.  Bump this up, and modify
   /etc/dt/config/sys.dtwmrc or $HOME/.dt/dtwmrc
to add keypress or mouse clicks to advance to next or previous
workspace.  Read man page for dtwm, and see the resources to set to
set up default backgrounds for the workspaces on other heads.  We've
been using the background menu to invoke apps.  The DISPLAY is set for
the display that the menu was invoked on.

We've been running 3-headed Dec OSF unix for over a year, getting good
reviews.  Hope this helps.

Cheers,
-Bob Arendt




