what PC's in general and MS in particular have done to all of us.  No, there was
never a strong market for the strong ox, but there were/are jobs that only the
strong ox can do.  The conversation goes something like this:

PHB: You want how much for a computer to predict the weather?  Ha!  Look at my
computer, does letters and everything else I want.  Your old Cray couldn't even
do letters.  Still, to keep you happy, I'll get you 2 new PCs, that ought to
solve your problems.

Scientist: (Says nothing, it doesn't matter since what he needs no longer is
produced. At least he can use the PC to re-do his resume.)

Things like medicine are getting into computers much more these days.  Might
even use them during important operations.  Wonder what happens to the patient
who is lucky enough to draw the BSOD, at a critical point?

