Synopsys Design Compiler. VHDL/Verilog simulation (Verilog-XL,
VCS, ModelSim, ...)

All commercial programs, which doesn't care much for 1024 chickens.
But the strong oxen, bring it over here please!

I'm not saying you cannot parallelize these tasks, just that no
commercial tools exists (that I know of).

Regression test suites can benefit from the 1024 chickens, but
back end stuff (e.g. top-level synthesis, timing reports, etc) won't.

Some of us don't write our own programs - we've got better things to do,
like designing ASICs (as I do). We must rely on the software we can get,
and whining about the tool doesn't support splitting the task out on the
N CPUs in the box wont help me here and now, and it only *might* help
me some years into the future (some of the tool vendors are known to
be rather, uhm, slow in responding to customer requests).

