In article <385A6998.3DEFD260@discovery.fuentez.com>,
Jim Jennis  <jjennis@discovery.fuentez.com> wrote:
> Hi Digital Unix Colleagues!
> 
> We are running ssh on linux and have just installed it (ssh v1.2.27) on
> digital unix v5.0 (shortly we will also install FISH/SSH on a new VMS
> machine). SSH compiled fine on Alpha/Tru64 with no errors, however, when
> we try to connect to the Alpha box from Linux (or any other ssh client),
> sshd on the Alpha hangs at the encryption type.

Did you change the rsaref code so that it uses ints instead of longs for
its 32 bit wide data?  Look in rsaref2/source/global.h, and see how big
a UINT4 is.  If it's unsigned long, it's wrong on the alpha.  You'll want to
patch it to use unsigned ints on the alpha, and you'll also want to apply
the recent buffer overflow patch too (see CERT's web site).

I've heard of performance problems with 1.2.27 on Digital/Tru64 Unix, so
we've mostly stuck with 1.2.26.  It seems to work fine on Tru64 5.0, as long
as you compile it on 5.0.

Tim
