Darek,

Should go something like this (assuming you intialize the logical raid
unit in the RCU program and its seen on boot as
re0).

./MAKEDEV re0
disklabel -wr re0 SWXCR  (or UNKOWN on 4.0D to query the disk)
disklabel -e re0

Your partition c should correspond to length of the logical device re0.
No editing of disktab is necessary;  specifying SWXCR or re should
write the correct label.. querying the logical raid unit for the size.
It didn't seem to work for you;  the label you have shows it. Try
a disklabel -z to zero the broken label out and try again.  You could
also try a manual disklabel edit (with the correct size); here's
one of mine for a 4Gb mirror.   Good luck.

