Jure Simsic <jure.simsic@uni-lj.si> wrote:

: I couldn't find any updated disktab anywhere and the DU faqs say that
: disklabel should be able to figure it out for itself when there's no
: entry in the disktab.. 
: Disktab also says it's SCSI when it should be IDE, but

I know it only from scsi disks:

disklabel -z /dev/rrz16a
disklabel -rw /dev/rrz16a dummy

If  choose  a  name  which is unknown in the disktab file then disklabel
command will ask the disk for the geometry. This values you can show and
the partitions can be set with:

disklabel -re /dev/rrz16a

HTH 
