> Don't cluster-wannabes resemble more NFS servers than actual clusters ?
> 
> I don't beleive that cluster-wannabes do volume-shadowing across nodes, do
> they ?

Most UNIX "clusters" are interconnected by little more than NFS (what's
in that little depends on the vendor).  TruCluster on Tru64 (formerly
Digital) UNIX uses a VMS-like distributed lock manager, and coordinates
disk access via that DLM.  It would be interesting to find out what
protocol TruCluster's DLM runs over.

