Yes you can install all the patches. Once it prompts you to enter the top
level of the patch directory i.e lets say that you have the patches in a
directory called /patches and then you do a dupatch it will ask you to enter
the top level directory of the patches. so you can give the top level
directory. Before you install the patches it will ask you whether you want
to be able to undo the patches and it will also prompt you to confirm the
patches you want to install. If you dont confirm you can exit the
installation. The complete thing is menu driven and you can get back to the
main menu and exit the installation. Are you seeing the menu at all? I think
the command you are giving tries to install all the patches at once. So,
just invoke dupatch and then try installing the patches. Even before that
you can select to do a pre-patch inspection of the system. This is one of
the options in the menu.Hope this helps.

Narasimha

