I don't really know if this is a Fortran or T64 question so I'll start
here.  We have an XP1000, T64 v4.0F, Fortran 5.2 in for evaluation.
The guy who's doing the testing has a Fortran code that opens a file
for direct writes of very large records.  He claims there's a
significant delay when the code issues the write statement, as if
the code has to wait for the i/o to be written to disk.  He's
comparing this system with an AIX system where it appears the write
statement causes the record to be written to some internal buffer
and his code continues executing while the data is actually written
to disk.  The result is that the elapsed time for the code on the
alpha is significantly more than for the AIX system, even though the
cpu time of the alpha is the same or less.

If this were a VMS system I'd have lots of ideas about how to
investigate this, what to change, etc. to reduce the elapsed run
time.   But, obviously this isn't VMS.  Can someone give me some
ideas about what to look at for a T64 system?

Thanks,
Dave
