brandon chubb wrote:

> Does anyone know if the ld flags -hidden and -hidden_symbol still work?
> It seems to completely ignore them..if anyone's used them and can
> give me a command line example I'd be much appreciative.  Any symbols
> I hand to -hidden_symbol still show up from 'nm'.

The -hidden and -hidden_symbol linker flags work fine.  They only work for
shared libraries.
The "nm" utility doesn't understand hidden symbols since hidden symbols
are only related
to shared libraries and used by the runtime loader.

If you use "odump -Dtv your_lib.so" to dump your library's symbols, you'll
see the hidden
symbols marked LOCAL rather than GLOBAL.

Joe Mario




